cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RiverSynth in teaching, research, talks, art or media, please cite it as below."
title: "RiverSynth: turn river flow into music"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Cognac
    given-names: Kristen
abstract: >-
  RiverSynth is a free browser synthesizer and science-communication tool that turns
  real USGS stream-gauge data into music, so people can listen to how rivers rise,
  fall, flood and run dry.
repository-code: "https://github.com/KECognac/RiverSynth"
url: "https://kecognac.github.io/RiverSynth/"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-10-15"
keywords:
  - sonification
  - streamflow
  - hydrology
  - science communication
  - synthesizer
  - web audio
